[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "1. Contract term",
    "text": "i. The Times and the Union agree to a new Contract (the \"Contract™) for a term of six years from March 31, 1987 to March 30, 1993. The Contract shall be the present contract with the changes made by this Memorandum of Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "2(a). 1987–1988 wage increases and contributions",
    "text": "2. The Wage Rate and Cost-of-Living Adjustment provisions of the Contract shall be as follows: (a) Effective March 31, 1987, the weekly journeyman day scale shall be increased by $43.35 a week. Pension and welfare contributions shall be made on this amount. Effective March 31, 1987, an additional §3.67 per shift from wages and after taxes (maximum of five (5) shifts) shall be contributed to the Welfare Fund. Payments retroactive to March 31, 1987 shall be made no later than thirty (30) days from the date of ratification of this Memorandum of Agreement. Effective March 31, 1988, the weekly journeyman day scale shall be increased by $35 a if FUNDO0001069 week. Payments retroactive to March 31, 1988 shall be made no later than thirty (30) days fron the date of ratification of this Memorandum of Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "2(b). Subsequent wage increases",
    "text": "(b) The weekly journeyman day scale shall be increased by $43 a week on March 31, 1989; by '$40 a week on March 31, 1990; by $36 a week on March 31, 1991; and by $36 — a week on March 3], 1992."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "2(c). Cost-of-living adjustments",
    "text": "(C) Cost of living adjustments shall be made effective March 31, 1988, March 31, 1989, March 31, 1990, March 31, 1991, and March 31, 1992, pursuant to the relevant provisions of the Contract. [The Bureau of Labor Statistics (BLS) Consumer Price Index (1967 = 100) (CPI-W) for New York, New York = Northeastern New Jersey (Index) hall be used for measurement of the change.)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "3. New and rebuilt facilities",
    "text": "3. The Times and the Union agree that the Contract shall have full force and effect at the Edison, New Jersey by The Times within the Northeast Corridor (Maine te Northern Virginia). Because of the magnitude of the investment in new and rebuilt plants The Times is Planning and its importance to the future of the business and the security of the members of the Union, The Times and the Union are committed to the orderly, successful and efficient start-up and operation of the new and rebuilt plants. The af FUNDO0001070 Times and the Union therefore reaffirm that any dispute concerning the interpretation and application of the Contract, including any dispute concerning the interpretation and application of the Contract at anew or rebuilt facility, shall be resolved through the Contract's grievance and arbitration procedure. Without limiting the disputes to be resolved pursuant to the Contract's grievance and arbitration procedure, the parties intend to resolve all questions that may arise from innovations in methods of operation, as for example operations with palletizing equipment, by discussion and arbitration if necessary, it being understood that notwithstanding the introduction of any such new methods, the Contract will continue to protect regular situation holders against layoffs for the term of the Contract because of the introduction of automated processes. The Times agrees that all such protected regular situation holders shall be listed by name on the date of ratification and on the date of the commencement of built facility. With respect to a eee Ee i ot ate é ae at tae he & erations at any ne the commencement of operations at any new or rebuilt facility, every effort shall be made to place employees in jobs most nearly equivalent to the work peformed in current operations. It is further agreed that to the extent practicable regular situation holders engaged in advance product production at Carlstadt shall constitute the initial work force at Edison."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "3. Pre-operation arbitration and mediation",
    "text": "In connection with any arbitration concerning the interpretation and application of the Contract at @ new or rebuilt facility, the arbitrator shall issue his award before operations commence. Should the arbitrator fail to issue his award before operations at a new or rebuilt facility begin, operations shall commence under operating conditions established in an interim ruling by the arbitrator and shall continue thus until the arbitrator issues his award. Upon the written request of either party, the parties agree to attempt to resolve any issues under | this paragraph prior to arbitration through non-binding mediation by a mutually agreed upon mediator. The use of mediation shall not delay any arbitration proceeding on any euch issues."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "4. Adoption of other unions' wage packages",
    "text": "4. If, in connection with any collective bargaining “: agreement, letter agreement, side agreement or memoranda of agreement now effective or which later becomes effective through and including March 30, 1993 or any shorter period, The Times agrees with any labor organization (Electricians, Guild, Machinists, Mailers, Paperhandlers, Photo-Engravers, Pressmen, Stereotypers, Typographers) representing The Times! employees upon @ wage and benefit package which is additional to or different from that contained herein, the Union may, at its option, adopt such increased wage and benefit package, provided that such increased wages and benefits have not been granted in exchange for productivity ta FUNDO0001072 improvements or attrition, or have not been diverted fron an. existing or subsequently negotiated wage and benefit package. Any dispute about the application of thie Paragraph shall be resolved through Contract 's grievance and arbitration procedure."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "5(a). Welfare Fund administration",
    "text": "5. (a) In the event the Publishers’ Association of New York City shall no longer act as agent for The Times with respect to the Publishers'-Newspaper and Mail Deliverers' Welfare Fund, The Times hall cause its duly _ authorized officers to enter into such agreements and execute such documents, including but not limited te group contracts and trust agreements and amendments thereto, as are necessary to administer the Publishers'-Newspaper and Mail Deliverers' Welfare Fund."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "5(b). Pension Fund administration",
    "text": "(b) In the event the Publishers! Association of - New York City shall no longer act ag agent for The Times with respect to the Newspaper and Mai} Delivererg'= Publishers: Pension Fund, The Times shall cause its duly authorized officers to enter into such agreements and execute such documents, including but not limited to the Pension Plan and corresponding trust agreement and amendments thereto, aS Ore necessary to administer the Newspaper and Mail Deliverers'-Publisherg! Pension Fund,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "5(c). Fund-expenditure limitation",
    "text": "(C¢) Nothing in this paragraph 5 shall be construed to require The Times to expend any funds beyond its obligation to make contributions required by the Contract for The Times Geliverers to the Welfare Fund and the Pension Fund."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "6. Shop-dispute resolutions",
    "text": "6. Various shop disputes are resolved as set forth in Appendix A to this Memorandum of Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "7. Nondiscrimination",
    "text": "“There shall be no discrimination in hiring or in any other condition of employment by reason of color, race, sex, religion or national origin.\""
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "8. Accidental death and dismemberment coverage",
    "text": "é. Effective upon ratification of this Memorandum of Agreement, the Accidental Death and Dismemberment Insurance Coverage provided for in Section 3-H.2 of the Collective Bargaining Agreement shall be increased from $60,000 to $75,000."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "9. Jury-service pay",
    "text": "9. Effective upon the ratification of this Memorandum of Agreement, Group I employees not so scheduled shall be paid for jury service based upon the number of days per week that he or she worked during the eight weeks prior to reporting for jury service. Section l3-J = Jury Service of ii FUNDO001074 the Collective Bargaining Agreement shall be amended to reflect this change."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "10. Plant foremen",
    "text": "\"Whenever the Publisher has one or more Plants, there shall be a foreman or * assistant foreman in each plant.\""
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "11. Welfare Fund contribution letter",
    "text": "dl. The Times will provide the Union with a letter regarding weekly contributions to the Welfare Fund, attached as Appendix € to this Memorandum of Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "12. Section 3-P interpretation letter",
    "text": "12. The Times will provide the Union with a letter regarding The Times' interpretation of Contract Section 3-P as set forth in the 1981-84 Cellective Bargaining Agreement, attached as Appendix D to this Memorandum of Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "13. Arbitrator-designation letter",
    "text": "13. The Times and the Union agree to execute a letter of understanding regarding the designations of \"Status Quo\" and Merits Arbitrators, attached as Appendix E to this Menorandum of Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "14. Continuing agreements and precedence",
    "text": "14. All letter agreements, side agreements, supplementary agreements, memoranda of agreement and | memoranda of understanding in effect on the date hereof, and all terms and conditions contained in the 1981-84 contract i FUNDO001075 booklet, shall remain in full force and effect unless modified by this Memorandum of Agreement. All dates in the Contract shall be updated to reflect this Memorandum of Agreement. If any conflict occurs between the terms of this Memorandum of Agreement and any other agreement, the terms of this Memorandum of Agreement shall prevail."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "15. Preparation of new contract document",
    "text": "15. Promptly after execution of this Memorandum of Agreement, the parties shall prepare and execute a complete new contract document (The New York Times Agreement) embodying the provisions contained in the Contract as modified to reflect and effectuate the changes agreed to herein."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "16. Effective date",
    "text": "16. This Memorandum of Agreement shall be effective immediately following Union ratification."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "Appendix A 1.A. Additional floor situations",
    "text": "ho pute Resolutions i. Subject to there being no increase in the number of floor hires as set forth in the Collective Bargaining Agreement, it is agreed that: A. Ten additional floor regular situations (Wednesday~Saturday days at the Carlstadt plant and Sunday night at the 43d Street plant) shall be created."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "Appendix A 1.B. Additional situations and chauffeurs",
    "text": "B. Five additional floor regular situations (Wednesday-Saturday night at the Carlstadt Plant and Sunday night at the 43d Street plant) shall be created and five additional chauffeurs on dayside (4 days and Monday night)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "Appendix A 2. Third recovery car",
    "text": "Ze One regular situation shall be created for the third recovery car."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "Appendix A 3. Jitney job bids",
    "text": "3. The jitney (\"Blue Googe\") work as set forth in pages 104-5 of the 1981-4 Collective Bargaining Agreement shall be updated to reflect the names of the two employees that presently hold these job bids."
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "Home Delivery Copies",
    "text": "Obe Pelive Opies Home delivery copies shall continue to be served by having routemen deliver papers for one or more home delivery dealers, agents, or TeRoute contractors to delivery points designated by the Publisher at which the Papers will be picked up and delivered to the home delivery customers by the home delivery Gealers, agents or T-Route contractors,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c027",
    "name": "West Side Direct Routes",
    "text": "The present Memorandum of Agreement on \"West Side Direct Routes\" entered into on November 22, 1983 shall be abolished and The Times shall have the right to reorganize these routes, provided the present number of routes in the West Side Direct operation Shall not be reduced during the term of this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c028",
    "name": "Honor Boxes and Vending Machines reference",
    "text": "With respect to Honor Boxes and Vending Machines, se. Appendix B-1."
  },
  {
    "id": "c029",
    "name": "Returns",
    "text": "All returns, except unsold current coples on *bulldog* routes, shall be handled by the dealers' wailing to the Publisher the headsheet or other designated portion of each copy for counting and order regulation by the Publisher or its designee. Any existing physical pick-up of such copies shall continue for the duration of this Contract."
  },
  {
    "id": "c030",
    "name": "Appendix B. Honor Boxes and Vending Machines",
    "text": "This side-letter confirms that with respect to Honor Boxes and Vending Machines The Times and the Union agree to maintain present Practices in such deliveries in The Times direct operation,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c031",
    "name": "Weekly Welfare Fund contributions",
    "text": "Within 30 days after ratification, contributions to the Welfare Fund (Publishers'-Newspaper and Mail Deliverers' Welfare Fund) shall be made weekly. Such payments for any payroll week shall be made available no later than ten (10) days following the end of such payroll week."
  },
  {
    "id": "c032",
    "name": "Section 3-P interpretation",
    "text": "The Union has asked that The Times Clarify its interpretation of the terms \"Grandfather\" and \"Grandmother\" as used in Section 3-P of the Contract, polnting out that the terms have not always been interpreted and applied consistently. This will confirm that these terns mean the Grandfather or Grandmother of a Regular Situation Holder or Group I Extra or of his or her spouse at the time the grandparent dies."
  },
  {
    "id": "c033",
    "name": "Section 3-P nonretroactivity",
    "text": "This letter shall not have retroactive effect, and shall not be used or referred to in Support of any claim for leave under Section 3-P on account of a death occurring prior to the date hereof."
  },
  {
    "id": "c034",
    "name": "Accumulation of leave days",
    "text": "\"An employee may elect to accumulate a ll ef hi yt 2t AY OF & ee ee oe leave days\" and ’ Yy GF ii OF Mis unused"
  },
  {
    "id": "c035",
    "name": "Neutral-designation process",
    "text": "The parties have identified certain neutrals subject to their availability and Willingness to serve, and will meet within sixty (60) days of ratification to effectuate the designation process."
  },
  {
    "id": "c036",
    "name": "Atlantic City",
    "text": "Atlantie city The Times shall negotiate the conditions for establishing a run to Atlantic City when the normal daily order reaches 2500 copies."
  },
  {
    "id": "c037",
    "name": "Glen Burnie/Lancaster arrangements",
    "text": "Glen Burnie/Lancaster The Times and the Union will discuss and identify the present problems concerning the transport of The Times! existing Television Magazine from Glen Burnie, Maryland to The Times's Carlstadt er Edison, New Jersey plant. After The Times and the NMDU have agreed upon satisfactory arrangements for the transport of The Times' Television Magazine and such arrangements are in operation, but no jater than thirty (30) days from the date the revised Glen - Burnie agreement has been put into effect, The Times will assign to employees represented by the NMDU a Nonday delivery of The Times Magazine printed in Lancaster, Pennsylvania to The Times’ plant in Carlstadt or Edison, New Jersey. The conditions for the delivery of the Monday run shall not involve The Times in increased costs,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c038",
    "name": "Additional Lancaster transportation",
    "text": "After The Times and the Union have resolved satisfactorily any grievances, differences and disputes with respect to the work to be performed by employees represented iF] FUNDO0001084 by the NMDU at the Edison, New Jersey plant and the staffing and other conditions applicable to such work and the Edison plant is running, The Times will negotiate with the NMDU the arrangements pursuant to which Times employees represented by the NMDU will transport additional portions of The Times Magazine printed in Lancaster, Pennsylania to The Times! plant in Edison, New Jersey, providing such transport does not involve The Times in increased costs."
  },
  {
    "id": "c039",
    "name": "Section 13-H.1(a). Welfare contribution percentage",
    "text": "Revise Section 13-H.1 of the 1981-84 collective bargaining agreement: as follows: (a) Change \"6-1/2%\" to \"7.678%\" to reflect the present welfare contribution percentage and"
  },
  {
    "id": "c040",
    "name": "Section 13-H.1(b). After-tax deduction",
    "text": "(b) add “and an after tax deduction from wages of $3.67 after the words \"per shift\" in the first sentence and"
  },
  {
    "id": "c041",
    "name": "Section 13-H.1(c). Casual Welfare Fund contributions",
    "text": "(c) dncrease the additional contributions for casuals to the Welfare Fund as follows: 3/31/87 = §.00 per shift . 3/31/88 - 10.00 \" 3/31/89 - 11.00 v 3/31/90 - 12.00 \" 3/31/91 - 13.00 \" 3/31/92 - 14.00"
  },
  {
    "id": "c042",
    "name": "Section 9B. Sixty-day written notice",
    "text": "Amend Bection 9B dnsert after the words, “notify the Union\" in the last sentence: \"in writing, at least Sixty (60) days prior thereto\" [balance as in original)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c043",
    "name": "Section 9B. Notice scope and exception",
    "text": "Add to the end of the Paragraph, \"This ghali only apply to a New York Times part or section regularly inserted in the Sunday or daily newspaper. It is understood that the _Bixty (60) day notice to the Union shall not be required if The Times can demonstrate that it did not have sixty (60) days' notice itself in which event it Shall give the Promptest practicable notice to the Union. This does not “modi fy any other notice requirements pursuant to the Contract.”"
  },
  {
    "id": "c044",
    "name": "Vacation-pay diversion",
    "text": "The Times agrees that on or after March 31, 1990 the Union may divert a uniform portion of each employee's wage increase to become effective then or thereafter to a vacation pay benefit."
  },
  {
    "id": "c045",
    "name": "Diversion cost and cooperation",
    "text": "It is agreed that such diversion shall not result in any increase in cost to The Times other ‘an nominal administrative costs and that The Times will fully cooperate with the Union in developing any such alternatives and researching the financial details thereof."
  },
  {
    "id": "c046",
    "name": "Terminally ill employees committee",
    "text": "The parties will establish a committee of two (2) Times and two (2) NMDU represenatives to study possible methods of assisting terminally 111 employees represented by the NMDU."
  },
  {
    "id": "c047",
    "name": "Saturday Night Bulldog",
    "text": "‘Baturday Night Bulldog The Times agrees that go long as it has a Saturday night Bulldog Edition ) it will guarantee all Saturday night Bulldog uding routes and relays)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c048",
    "name": "Earnings Bonus 1. 1987 bonus",
    "text": "1. It is acknowleged that The Times has already paid the Earnings Bonus for 1987 at the rate of 5.112% of the gross wages paid such employees in 1987 notwithstanding any provision to the contrary and will not seek to recalculate said bonus or to seek credit or set-off for the amounts paid, except that it is understood and agreed that no Earnings Bonus shall be paid for the retroactive wages for 1987 paid in 1988 for the general increase effective March 31, 1987."
  },
  {
    "id": "c049",
    "name": "Earnings Bonus 2. 1988–1992 rate",
    "text": "2. _For calendar years 1988, 1989, 1990, 1991 ana 1992, the Earnings Bonus will be 3.86% of the gross wages paid the employee by The Tines Guring the applicable year."
  },
  {
    "id": "c050",
    "name": "Earnings Bonus 3. 1993 rate",
    "text": "Je For the period January 1, 1993 through March 30, 1993, the Earnings Bonus wil} be 3.86% of the gross wages paid the employee by The Times during such pericd."
  },
  {
    "id": "c051",
    "name": "Earnings Bonus 4(a). Gross wages definition",
    "text": "4. (a) “Gross wages\" means compensation reported as “wages, tips and other compensation\" on the employee's W-2 Form for the applicable bonus period, excluding any Earnings Bonus received during that bonus period and for calendar year 1988 excluding any retroactive wages for 1987 paid in 1988 for the general increase effective March 31, 1987, The Earnings Bonus shal] be reported on a separate W-2 Form."
  },
  {
    "id": "c052",
    "name": "Earnings Bonus 4(b). Disability and compensation benefits",
    "text": "(b) However, with regard to those shifts for which an employee receives benefits under The Times Disability Plan, the employee's state disability benefit or workers' compensation benefit for such shifts shall be added to the employee's gross wages for purposes of calculating the employee's Earnings Bonus, to the extent that guch State disability and workers! compensation benefits do Not appear on the employee's W-2 Forn."
  },
  {
    "id": "c053",
    "name": "Earnings Bonus 5. Payment deadline",
    "text": "5, The Earnings Bonus shall be paid within 60 Gays after the end of the applicable bonus period."
  },
  {
    "id": "c054",
    "name": "Earnings Bonus 6. Post-1993 disposition",
    "text": "6. The continuation or other disposition of the Earnings Bonus after March 30, 1993 shall be Getermined by negotiations between The Times and the Union in accordg with the Contract, except that if the Parties have not agreed by March 30, 1993 on the continuation Or other disposition of the Earnings Bonus after March 30, 1993, effective March 31, 1993 the Earnings Bonus shai] cease and $25.93 at the Union's option shall be added to the weekly wage scales or allocated in the manner set forth in Paragraph 7. The Earnings Bonus due for the period January 1, 1993 through March 30, 1993 shall be paid, if not continued, within thirty (30) days after March 30, 1993,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c055",
    "name": "Earnings Bonus 7. Union termination right",
    "text": "7. The Union reserves the right during the tern of the Contract, on thirty (30) days notice to The Times, to terminate these Earnings Bonus provisions and apply $25.93 to the weekly wage scales or te any fringe benefit provided under the contract or negotiated by any other union and the Times in connection with the current extension negotiations Or at any time through March 39, 1993. Should the Union exercise this right, The Times Will pay, within Sixty (60) days of the date of termination, the Earnings Bonus due on 9rOSS wages for any prior bonus period."
  },
  {
    "id": "c056",
    "name": "Earnings Bonus 8. Wage-rate treatment",
    "text": "8. It is agreed that go long as this Earnings Bonus agreement applies, any benefit provided te employees by The Times pursuant to the Contract or otherwise which is calculated on or determined by the employee'¢ wage rate shall be calculated or determined as if the wage scales were increased by $25.93 per week. This provision Shall include by example, but not limitation, Times retirement or pension benefits, wick Pay and stock purchase options. Where a benefit such as Workers! Compensation, State Disability benefits or Unemployment Insurance requires a statement of wage rate, The Times will report the employee's wage rate as increased by $25.93 per week. This Paragraph shall be applied so as to eliminate any duplication of the Earnings benefit or wage rate. Further, nothing herein shall be construed to require The Times to make contributions to the FUNDO0001092 am ©} so Publishers '=NMDU Welfare Fund or NMDU-Publishers' Pension Fund on Earnings Bonus payments or to calculate such contributions as if the employee's wage scale were increased by $25.93 per week."
  },
  {
    "id": "c057",
    "name": "Four Man Board 1. Paragraph 3 number",
    "text": "1. The number in the first sentence of Paragraph 3 is now eighty-eight (88)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c058",
    "name": "Honor-box practices clarification",
    "text": "Pursuant to our discussions on the subject, I am enclosing for your records a copy of an internal memorandum from Joseph Spinelli to Andy Riggs. The memorandum describes the present practices regarding vending machines in the West Side Direct delivery Operation. These, therefore, are the practices continued by the side letter agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c059",
    "name": "Vending-machine present practice",
    "text": "In reply to your inquiry, the Present practice is that Vending Machines in our West Side Direct delivery area are served by dropping Papers for ali vending machines in that area (now 121) at three locations. Those three locations presently are (1) 4ist Street and 7th Avenue; (2) 66th and (3) 1924 Street ana Fort Washington Avenue. As the number of Street and West End Avenue; vending machines has increased, we have incorporated their delivery into one of the three locations."
  },
  {
    "id": "c060",
    "name": "West Side Directs clarification",
    "text": "This will confirm our understanding that the \"abolition\" of the November 22, 1983 \"Menorandum of Agreement\" Shall not affect any other agreement contained therein or otherwise regarding those routes other than that portion Providing for attrition of those routes,"
  }
]

