{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"The present contract\" is not identified by date or title, and the only contract booklet elsewhere referenced is the expired 1981-84 booklet (paragraph 14), so what body of terms the six-year \"Contract\" consists of is left open. The reader cannot tell from these words whether side letters and memoranda are part of the \"present contract\" or only preserved separately by paragraph 14.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.32}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The \"additional $3.67 per shift from wages and after taxes ... shall be contributed to the Welfare Fund\" does not say whose money it is — an employer contribution or an employee wage deduction remitted to the Fund — nor whether it is owed for shifts beyond the five-shift maximum. That characterization determines the size of the employer's contribution obligation.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.42},
     {"issue": "The same $3.67 is described in the Section 13-H.1 amendment (Appendix, \"add 'and an after tax deduction from wages of $3.67'\") as a deduction from wages rather than as a contribution to the Welfare Fund, and the two descriptions cannot both be given literal effect. A court asked how much is owed to the Fund would have to reconcile paragraph 2(a) with that amendment.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "Paragraph 2(a) expressly directs that \"Pension and welfare contributions shall be made on this amount\" for the 1987 increase, while paragraph 2(b) states the 1989-1992 increases with no such direction, inviting a negative-implication argument that contributions are not owed on them. The relationship between the two subparagraphs, not the figures, is what would be construed.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The clause fixes no formula, base period or multiplier for the cost-of-living adjustment, deferring wholly to unspecified \"relevant provisions of the Contract,\" and the bracketed Index sentence does not say whether the measurement runs May-to-May or January-to-January. The 1992 Memorandum's later stipulation that adjustments \"utilize a January to January rather than a May to May Index\" shows the gap.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The opening sentence is incomplete — \"shall have full force and effect at the Edison, New Jersey [gap] by The Times within the Northeast Corridor\" — so the class of facilities covered (Edison only, or every new or rebuilt plant in the Corridor) cannot be read off the words. The later garbled passage about listing protected regular situation holders leaves the same scope question open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.42}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Any issues under this paragraph\" has no fixed referent: the mediation sentence sits in a separate block from numbered paragraph 3, so it is unclear whether mediation reaches only new/rebuilt-facility arbitrations or all disputes under paragraph 3. The command that \"the arbitrator shall issue his award before operations commence\" is also stated as mandatory yet immediately assumes he may not.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The me-too right is keyed to \"any labor organization\" followed by a parenthetical list of nine named unions, leaving it open whether the list is exhaustive (expressio unius) or merely illustrative. \"Wage and benefit package\" is likewise undefined as against the productivity/attrition and diversion provisos.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The obligation is to execute such documents \"as are necessary to administer\" the Welfare Fund, an open-ended standard with an illustrative \"including but not limited to\" list, so what The Times must actually sign is undetermined. Whether that reaches the Fund's trust agreement and its delinquency machinery is left to argument.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "As with 5(a), the duty to execute documents \"as are necessary to administer\" the Pension Fund states no standard for necessity and no limit on the documents covered. The Fund's own trust agreement (Article 9) purports to govern rate, mode and enforcement of contributions, so what 5(b) commits The Times to is uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The disclaimer that nothing requires The Times \"to expend any funds beyond its obligation to make contributions\" is hard to square with the Fund trust agreement's Article 9.4, which imposes interest, liquidated damages and collection costs on a delinquent employer. A delinquency defendant would invoke 5(c) as capping its exposure at contributions alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011",
   "issues": [
